# The floppy intro's named dumpScreen checkpoints are captured as each scene
# completes (fast render, one frame per scene). The wait gives the fast
# pass enough real time to reach the throne room; keep the engine alive in
# the first room long enough for the audio window to prove the mixer is not
# silent.
wait 15000
checkpoint floppy-landing
checkpoint floppy-room-scripted
wait 5000
# Paul's head opens the globe with the game menu; SAVE GAME (third row)
# lists the four logs; the last row is EXIT GLOBE.
move 160 145
click left 160 145
wait 4000
checkpoint floppy-globe
move 160 179
click left 160 179
wait 1500
checkpoint floppy-menu-save
move 160 195
click left 160 195
wait 1500
# SEE DUNE MAP (the first row): the flat map with its DUNE MAP title popup
# (seg000:5bb0), the map menu (seg000:878c) and the planet in the left panel.
move 160 163
click left 160 163
wait 3000
checkpoint floppy-map-flat
move 160 163
click left 160 163
wait 1000
# Duke Leto's opening conversation: the second command row, then a tap per
# page (view area) until the throne room returns.
move 160 171
click left 160 171
wait 1500
checkpoint floppy-leto-1
move 160 80
click left 160 80
wait 1500
checkpoint floppy-leto-2
click left 160 80
wait 1500
checkpoint floppy-leto-3
click left 160 80
wait 1000
quit
